WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.352
Hello, and welcome to week five: split a multiplication.

2
00:00:06.352 --> 00:00:11.449
By the end, you will be able to multiply by splitting a number into tens and ones.

3
00:00:11.449 --> 00:00:14.046
Let's start.

4
00:00:15.196 --> 00:00:19.612
How many counters?

5
00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:22.259
Counting them one by one is slow.

6
00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:25.251
We will split the rows instead.

7
00:00:27.151 --> 00:00:30.680
Push a gap after the tenth counter in every row.

8
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:33.817
Pause the video and have a go.

9
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.882
No counter moves to another row.

10
00:00:44.882 --> 00:00:49.058
Every row of thirteen is now ten and three.

11
00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:57.936
Count each part: four rows of ten, then four rows of three.

12
00:00:57.936 --> 00:01:01.571
Pause the video and have a go.

13
00:01:10.221 --> 00:01:14.795
Both parts are in every row, so both are multiplied by four.

14
00:01:14.795 --> 00:01:17.601
Then add the two parts.

15
00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:25.457
Write it in the grid: ten and three across the top, four down the side.

16
00:01:25.457 --> 00:01:28.907
Pause the video and have a go.

17
00:01:37.557 --> 00:01:41.400
The grid is the same picture with the counters taken away.

18
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.448
Multiply every part, then add.

19
00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:53.188
Now nineteen times three in the grid: split nineteen into ten and nine.

20
00:01:53.188 --> 00:01:56.196
Pause the video and have a go.

21
00:02:04.846 --> 00:02:07.342
The same grid with new numbers.

22
00:02:07.342 --> 00:02:13.240
Ten times three equals thirty and nine times three equals twenty-seven;

23
00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.235
both parts are multiplied by three.

24
00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:20.818
Thirty plus twenty-seven equals fifty-seven.

25
00:02:22.718 --> 00:02:27.954
Find nineteen times three another way: make three rows of twenty,

26
00:02:27.954 --> 00:02:31.367
then take one counter off the end of every row.

27
00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:34.864
Pause the video and have a go.

28
00:02:43.514 --> 00:02:46.184
Twenty times three equals sixty.

29
00:02:46.184 --> 00:02:51.072
We took away one counter from each of three rows: three counters, not one.

30
00:02:51.072 --> 00:02:56.842
So nineteen times three equals sixty subtract three equals fifty-seven,

31
00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:59.431
the same answer as the grid.

32
00:02:59.431 --> 00:03:04.036
Nineteen is close to twenty, so this way is quicker.

33
00:03:05.936 --> 00:03:08.037
Here is a worked example.

34
00:03:08.037 --> 00:03:14.338
Split twenty-seven into tens and ones to work out twenty-seven times three.

35
00:03:15.588 --> 00:03:21.439
Twenty times three equals sixty and seven times three equals twenty-one;

36
00:03:21.439 --> 00:03:27.860
both parts are multiplied; sixty plus twenty-one equals eighty-one.

37
00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:29.323
Pause the video.

38
00:03:29.323 --> 00:03:31.960
Try the next one in your booklet.

39
00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.419
Now let's try a question together.

40
00:03:43.419 --> 00:03:48.563
Work out thirty-nine times three by starting with forty times three.

41
00:03:48.563 --> 00:03:51.920
Pause the video and have a go.

42
00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:04.459
Forty times three equals one hundred and twenty.

43
00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:10.694
Thirty-nine is one less than forty in every row, so take away one three:

44
00:04:10.694 --> 00:04:15.907
one hundred and twenty subtract three equals one hundred and seventeen.

45
00:04:15.907 --> 00:04:18.585
Well done if you got it.

46
00:04:20.485 --> 00:04:22.343
Now try it in your booklet.

47
00:04:22.343 --> 00:04:27.509
Remember: split one number into parts and multiply every part;

48
00:04:27.509 --> 00:04:30.795
the parts' answers add up to the whole answer.

49
00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:32.323
Good luck.
